{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"iconic-interested-snake","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Discovered while closing the map-staleness gap on [rebar:259b-b7da-a346-4785] (Gerrit 1394)\n\n259b now makes the capability map's **provenance** checkable: `run_metadata.json` derives the\nharness digest from the Dockerfile's `FROM` line instead of a hand-copied constant, and\n`docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` records the digest it was measured against, asserted against\nthat pin by `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py`. A re-pin now lands red until\nthe map is regenerated.\n\n## What that does NOT cover\n\nThe staleness gate keys on the **digest**. It detects \"these answers describe a different\nimage\". It cannot detect **\"these answers are wrong about THIS image\"** — and that is the\nfailure mode this epic has actually hit:\n\n* `docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` recorded that DC rejected a 255-char label. A dedicated live\n  cell later posted 254- and 255-char labels to the SAME pinned image and both were accepted.\n  The entry was retracted. The digest never changed, so no digest-based check could have caught\n  it.\n\nThe mechanism is that the map's answers are produced by an **agentic LLM run** summarising raw\nREST evidence. The evidence in `evidence.json` was correct; the *reading* of it was wrong. So\nthe map has a trust boundary at exactly the point the ticket wanted removed — 259b's own words:\n\"otherwise we have swapped 'discovering from the instance' for 'trusting a model', which is\nworse.\"\n\n## The shape of a fix (not prescribing it)\n\nA **deterministic, non-LLM re-measurement** pass: a script that reads the committed contract and\nre-asserts each claim with a fixed REST call and an exact comparison, exiting non-zero on\ndivergence — no model in the measurement path. `scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py`\n(bug 1019) is the existing precedent for a deterministic probe alongside the agentic map, and\n`_assert_project_capabilities` in `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py` is the precedent for\n\"declared contract, fail loudly on divergence\". The agentic run stays useful for DISCOVERY (open\nquestions, new checklist items); it just should not be the last word on a value the harness then\ndepends on.\n\n## Also recorded: one measurement gap left open by 259b\n\n`docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` notes the description/comment 32767 boundary is a **coverage\ngap** — `jira.text.field.character.limit=32767` was read from the instance, but a literal 32K+\npayload was never written, so the limit is confirmed as *configured*, not as *observed*. That\nneeds an amd64 live run; it cannot be settled from a dev worktree.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] every claim the harness DEPENDS on is re-assertable by a deterministic (no-LLM) pass whose\n      comparison is exact, and which exits non-zero on divergence\n- [ ] the pass is runnable against the pinned image on demand, and its failure message names the\n      committed claim that diverged\n- [ ] the description/comment ceiling is measured with a real over-limit payload and read-back,\n      closing the recorded coverage gap\n- [ ] the agentic map's role is documented as DISCOVERY, with the deterministic pass as the\n      authority for anything the harness relies on","id":"a9bd-6641-e603-42bc","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"The capability map's answers are LLM-summarised, so a wrong answer at an unchanged digest is still undetectable"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785884055478458001,"uuid":"44837f9b-e231-45e5-b39f-becb8e4fea12"}